      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "BETTER BE DONE (2) gets the clearest winning case after already placing in Open grade at Eagle Farm on debut, where she was beaten just under 2L after travelling well and finishing into the money. Her Doomben run last week was below that level, but it came in Saturday company and she tackles easier company now with Thompson taking over. DIP WITH THE HIP (3) also comes through Open grade and has the chance to improve second-up after leading on heavy ground at Eagle Farm before fading. The inside draw gives her every opportunity to show more. SWIM UP BAR (1) is the most interesting debutant and strips fitter for a Deagon trial. Lerena's booking adds another layer. PASITA (6) is another first starter off a Deagon trial, and while the race evidence is thin, her trial margin was not wide and she profiles as a sensible inclusion for the minor end of the main chances. KWINANA SPIRIT (4) is a likely improver and looks best of the rest.",
